  \\\"question\\\":\\\"Can a follower hold a committed configuration that was never committed and then truncate its log so that its latest configuration names a server with no configuration entry behind it, and what does it do with that configuration?\\\",\n   \\\"source_ids\\\":[\\\"process_config_committed\\\",\\\"truncation_reset_latest\\\",\\\"append_commit_update\\\",\\\"membership_doc_proposal\\\"],\n   \\\"hypothesis\\\":\\\"processConfigurationLogEntry advances the committed configuration to the previous latest configuration whenever it installs a new one, without checking that the previous one was actually committed, and the appendEntries truncation path resets the latest configuration to the committed one when the conflicting suffix reaches past latestIndex. If a follower appends a configuration entry the leader never commits and later truncates that entry away, its latest configuration can still name the servers from that entry.\\\",\n   \\\"discriminator\\\":\\\"A trace or probe that appends a configuration entry at a follower, leaves the leader's commit index below it, then forces the follower to truncate that index and compares the follower's latest configuration with the entries actually present in its log, together with what the follower then uses that configuration for (vote granting, election participation, lease counting).\\\"}]}\njson.dump(d,open('update.json','w'),indent=2,ensure_ascii=False); open('update.json','a').write('\\\\n')\nPY\n/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/.venv/bin/python -I -B -c \\\"import sys; sys.path.insert(0, '/home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/src'); from consensus_assurance.cli import main; raise SystemExit(main())\\\" validate --run /home/nitro/Desktop/consensus-assurance/runs/2026-10-15_12-22-18-hashicorp_raft-real-run --submission update.json 2>&1 | tail -2\"","aggregated_output":"{\"valid\": true, \"run_id\": \"2190c36cecef4055bdfd7441367c6e18\", \"elapsed_seconds\": 2553.3626726899965, \"diagnostics\": [], \"meaning\": \"Read-only validation of these bytes and saved state; no acceptance, execution or budget reservation\", \"no_change\": false, \"execution_requested\": false, \"effects\": [{\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"process_config_committed\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"truncation_reset_latest\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"append_commit_update\"}, {\"object\": \"sources\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"membership_doc_proposal\"}, {\"object\": \"investigations\", \"action\": \"create\", \"target\": \"@follower_committed_heuristic\"}]}\n","exit_code":0,"status":"completed"}}
{"type":"item.completed","item":{"id":"item_5","type":"agent_message","text":"{\"submission\":\"update.json\",\"summary\":\"Registered a new sourced lead on the configuration-history mechanism, and recorded a negative result about the documentation: docs/membership.md describes AddVoter as making a server staging and Staging as a promotion path, neither of which matches the current API, so it is a design proposal rather than a contract and I did not use it as normative support. The lead comes from the code — processConfigurationLogEntry advances the committed configuration to the previous latest configuration before installing the new one, without checking that the previous one was committed, while the appendEntries truncation path resets the latest configuration to that committed value — so I registered the question whether a follower can hold a latest configuration naming a server whose configuration entry is no longer in its log, and what it would then do with it, with a discriminator that traces or probes the appending, the withheld commit and the forced truncation together. Four source ranges were recorded for that trace, no defect is asserted yet, and no execution was requested; the four existing questions and their accounts are unchanged.\"}"}}
